  - displayName: Shiitake Mushroom
    prefab: {fileID: 8829377244055881403, guid: a6db174f9825c1a40b6851035a7d1faf, type: 3}
    thumbnailOverride: {fileID: 0}
    scientificName: Lentinula edodes
    description: 'The cap is light brown to reddish brown 5 to 10 cm across. It often
      has whitish scales towards the edge of the cap.

      The gills are white
      and turn brown when bruised / with age.

      The stem is whitish and often
      off-centre and curved.'
    habitat: Found in East and Southeast Asia on decaying trees.
    uses: Used in food, but it must be cooked thoroughly.
    lookAlikes: 'Funeral Bell: compared to the shiitake''s white spore print, it
      has a rusty-brown spore print.'
    quick_characteristics: "<b>Quick identifiers:</b>\r\n \r\nWhite spore print\r\nGrows
      on dead trees\r\nWhite flesh with pleasant mushroom smell"
  - displayName: Shiitake mushroom
    prefab: {fileID: 8829377244055881403, guid: 735ba9a73c846ad4d93ec1fd5956f26f, type: 3}
    thumbnailOverride: {fileID: 0}
    scientificName: 
    description: 'The cap is light brown to reddish brown 5 to 10 cm across. It It
      often has whitish scales towards the edge of the cap.

      The gills are
      white and turn brown when bruised / with age.

      The stem is whitish and
      often off-centre and curved.'
    habitat: Found in East and Southeast Asia on decaying trees.
    uses: Used in food, but it must be cooked thoroughly.
    lookAlikes: 'Funeral Bell: compared to the shiitake''s white spore print, it
