  - displayName: Suede bolete
    prefab: {fileID: 8829377244055881403, guid: e55dfc09304757947865d28a17b0fdab, type: 3}
    thumbnailOverride: {fileID: 0}
    scientificName: Xerocomus subtomentosus
    description: 'The cap is olive brown, tan or yellowish brown and velvety.

      The
      stem is pale yellowish to light brown and usually has coarse brownish ribs
      near the top. It does not have a fine white network.'
    habitat: Found in coniferous woods across Europe, North America and Asia.
    uses: 'Used in food, has a mild taste and quickly turns slimy in the pan. '
    lookAlikes: 'Red Cracked Bolete: Has red cracks on its cap especially after /
      during dry seasons.'
    quick_characteristics: "<b>Quick identifiers:</b>\r\n \r\nDry, velvety cap\r\nCracks
      in cap are yellow\r\nHas tubes and not gills"
  - displayName: Tricholoma matsutake
    prefab: {fileID: 8829377244055881403, guid: 140f9cf3e115172419716eddfc928b20, type: 3}
    thumbnailOverride: {fileID: 0}
    scientificName: Matsutake / Pine Mushroom
    description: 'It grows half-buried in the ground.

      The cap is 6 to 20
      cm across, brown with darker brown fibres and scales.

      The flesh is
      white.

      It has a spicy and cinnamon-like smell.'
    habitat: 'It can be found in pine trees mainly in East Asia, but can be found
      in Northern Europe as well.

      It is most often found among moss and lichen.'
    uses: Used in food, has great taste.
    lookAlikes: 'Amanita smithiana: It lacks matsutake''s distinct smell and has
      a brown spore print.'
    quick_characteristics: "<b>Quick identifiers:</b>\r\n \r\nStrong, spicy, cinnamon-like
      smell\r\nWhite spore print\r\nVery firm, doesn't crumble"
